.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt ARCANACTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm arcanactl
.Nd command-line client for arcana-agent
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -libxo Ar options
.Op Fl qt
.Op Fl c Ar uri
.Op Fl A Ar cafile Fl C Ar certfile Fl K Ar keyfile
.Op Fl N Ar name
.Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends one request to a
.Xr arcana-agent 8
and prints the answer.
Output goes through
.Xr libxo 3 ,
so
.Fl -libxo Ns = Ns Ar json
and the other styles work.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl A Ar cafile , Fl C Ar certfile , Fl K Ar keyfile
The certificate authority that issued the server's certificate, and
this client's certificate and key, for network URIs.
.It Fl c Ar uri
The daemon to talk to.
Default
.Ql unix:/var/run/arcana-agent.sock .
.It Fl N Ar name
The name the server's certificate must carry, when it differs from the
host in
.Ar uri .
.It Fl q
Queue the change as a job; see the end of the command list.
.It Fl t
Also print the trace: every library call, system call, file and
program the daemon used, with the programs' output.
.El
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm hello
Show the host.
.It Cm list Op Fl c
List running and configured jails.
With
.Fl c ,
only configured ones.
.It Cm start | stop | restart | kill Ar jail
Change the jail's state.
.Cm kill
removes the jail without running its stop scripts.
.It Cm address add | remove Oo Fl lnp Oc Oo Fl i Ar interface Oc Ar jail Ar address Ns Op / Ns Ar len
Add or remove an address:
.Fl l
in the running jail (the default),
.Fl p
in its configuration file,
.Fl n
only showing what would change.
.Fl i
names the interface for the alias when the jail has no
.Va interface
parameter.
.It Cm services
The host's rc.d scripts: whether
.Xr rc.conf 5
enables them, and for the enabled ones whether they run, as
.Xr service 8
reports.
.It Cm service Ar name Cm start | stop | restart | reload | enable | disable
Change a service:
.Cm start ,
.Cm stop ,
.Cm restart
and
.Cm reload
through
.Xr service 8 ,
.Cm enable
and
.Cm disable
by setting its rcvar with
.Xr sysrc 8 .
.It Cm service Ar name Cm config Oo Fl x Ar key Oc ... Oo Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value Oc ...
The service's
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables, with what the script says of itself and its extra commands.
.Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value
sets one first,
.Fl x
unsets one; only the service's own variables are accepted.
.It Cm net routes | nexthops | connections | sockets Op Fl 4 | Fl 6
The host's routing table
.Pq Nm netstat Fl rnW ,
nexthop table
.Pq Nm netstat Fl onW ,
active connections
.Pq Nm netstat Fl nW
or open sockets
.Pq Nm sockstat Fl w ,
as the program printed them with
.Fl -libxo Cm json ,
for one address family or both.
.It Cm stats
CPU busy share since the previous request, load averages, memory, swap
and the ZFS pools.
.It Cm packages Oo Fl r Oc Op Ar jail
Packages of the host, or of the running
.Ar jail ,
that the repository has newer versions of
.Pq Nm pkg version Fl vRl '<' ;
.Fl r
fetches the catalogue first
.Pq Nm pkg update .
.It Cm pkg-upgrade Oo Fl n Oc Oo Fl j Ar jail Oc Op Ar package ...
.Nm pkg upgrade Fl y
of the named packages, or of all of them, on the host or in the running
.Ar jail ;
.Fl n
only shows what would be done.
What is still pending follows.
.It Cm jobs
The host's queued, running and recently finished jobs.
.It Cm job Oo Fl w Oc Ar id
One job with the trace of what it has done so far;
.Fl w
waits until it has finished.
.It Cm job-cancel Ar id
Take a job that has not started out of the queue.
.It Cm agent-update Oo Fl r Oc Ar program
Put
.Ar program
in place of the host's
.Xr arcana-agent 8 .
The host checks it against its SHA-256 and by running it with
.Fl V
before it replaces the one installed, which it keeps with the suffix
.Pa .old .
With
.Fl r
the service is restarted; otherwise the new program runs from its next
start.
.El
.Pp
With
.Fl q ,
.Cm start ,
.Cm stop ,
.Cm restart ,
.Cm kill ,
.Cm address ,
.Cm service
actions and variable changes, and
.Cm pkg-upgrade
are queued as a job instead of waited for:
.Nm
prints the job's number and returns.
The host runs its jobs one after another in the order they were queued,
whether or not anyone stays connected, which is what a change that cuts
the connection it was asked over needs.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the request succeeded, 1 when it failed, 2 for usage errors.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# arcanactl list
NAME             STATE     JID ADDRESSES                       HOSTNAME
web              running     3 10.0.0.10,10.0.0.11             web.lab.example
# arcanactl -t restart web
# arcanactl address add -lp web 10.0.0.12
# arcanactl -c tcp://host1:4310 -A ca.pem -C me.pem -K me.key list
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libxo 3 ,
.Xr arcana-agent 8 ,
.Xr arcana-console 8 ,
.Xr arcana-enrol 8 ,
.Xr jailconf 8
.Sh BUGS
.Xr libxo 3
writes tab characters into JSON strings unescaped, so JSON output
containing them, such as program output in a trace, is not strictly
valid JSON.
